  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g1210244-d2280662-r886942642-Charlestown_Executive_Apartments-Charlestown_Lake_Macquarie_Greater_Newcastle_N.html",
  "title": "A very poor show!",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "We will never book there again. After booking a Charlestown executive apartment 2 months in advance so our family from all over Queensland would be in the same location close to our son's party venue at Whitebridge, we were notified by a text with address and a code number for an apartment in Cardiff,  as we got off our plane at 3:30pm on Thursday 13th April.  The company didn't even call to say there was a problem. We called to say this wasn't where we'd booked and not a suitable arrangement but were told it was unavoidable. As it was 6 km further out than Charlestown, extra cost for taxi travel was incurred and our chance to get free transport with our family to and from Whitebridge wasn't an option as we were not in the same place.\nAfter terrible accommodation at Cardiff, with constant traffic noise, no lights on the high stairs, water running all over the bathroom from the shower and no coffee or sugar supplied, we cancelled the rest of our stay there. As there was no accommodation available at Charlestown on Friday night, we went elsewhere. We were then offered an available room for Saturday night, 15th, so we accepted that as we were close to the party venue and family as we'd planned.\nI enquired about a refund for the room that we cancelled on Friday night but was told that it wouldn't be refunded as we were offered a room at Cardiff, which wasn't where we'd booked in the first place. \nSo, all said and done, don't expect to get a room where you book with this company and be prepared for sub-standard apartments and no service.\nOur family got their apartments but one of our daughters' apartments was filthy when she and her family arrived as it hadn't been cleaned and there were putrid baby's nappies still there. At 4:30pm they had to wait for a cleaner to come before they could move in.\nThis fiasco cost us a heap more than it should have and we are very dissatisfied. \nCharlestown Executive Apartments showed very poor form and we didn't get what we booked or paid for.  ",
  "username": "903debral",
  "connectionToSubject": null,
  "absoluteUrl": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g1210244-d2280662-r886942642-Charlestown_Executive_Apartments-Charlestown_Lake_Macquarie_Greater_Newcastle_N.html",
