  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g1210244-d2280662-r835405865-Charlestown_Executive_Apartments-Charlestown_Lake_Macquarie_Greater_Newcastle_N.html",
  "title": "Great, with some improvements would be excellent",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "We stayed in a 2 bedroom plus (or 3 bedroom) apartment, husband and I, our daughter and husband’s parents. Unit #7, which was at the back and away from the traffic. \n\nWhen we arrived it was easy to get in, was provided a PIN code by text so didn’t have to line up to check in. Instructions were to park in the single garage, but unfortunately our Ford Ranger Ute didn’t fit. We wouldn’t have been able to close the garage door. Grandparents parked their Mazda 3 and had plenty of room and we found street parking right out the front. \n\nBedrooms were as described on the website. Grandparents and daughter took upstairs  2 bedrooms as we didn’t want our little one so far away from us during the night. Husband and I had the extra bedroom downstairs, which wasn’t a problem. Everyone had to walk through it on our way in and out but it was really no fuss. We all went to bed at the same time and it was quiet, despite there being no dedicated door to the ground floor. The stairs were a bit hard to get used to for people who aren’t used to them, but they were as described. Would not recommend for folks who may struggle. Ceilings appeared to be quite high, which meant lots of stairs! Would not recommend if you’d struggle with that. Baby gates were supplied, which would have been handy with little ones. \n\nThe not so good:\n- when we arrived and opened the garage door, we saw a number of cockroaches scatter. There were a few around the apartment which I believe is fairly normal for the area\n- the place was very dusty, you could see quite a thick layer on the floors coming up the stairs. Lots of dust bunnies where it could gather, under the furniture and around the stair railings.\n- carpet didn’t appear to be vacuumed on the top floor when we arrived. \n- some dirty dishes, glasses, mugs and cutlery\n\nWould have expected cleaning staff pay a bit more attention to detail or be given more time to be thorough. All in all, good value as it was quite cheap.",
